relate-query-latency: the graph-benchmark-ldbc workload (ADR-0243) and the QPP/LDBC corpus (ADR-0479)
===========================================================================================================

This crate's `graph-benchmark-ldbc` workload derives its queries and expected answers from prrao87/graph-benchmark-ldbc
(https://github.com/prrao87/graph-benchmark-ldbc) at commit c8eb87f6fba78aa8658036df2e1ca42377e254ac (2026-09-30):

  - workloads/graph-benchmark-ldbc/queries/q01.cypher ... q30.cypher: the 30 Cypher queries of neo4j/query.py, verbatim (dedented,
    trailing `;` dropped), each headed by a comment holding the function's docstring.
  - workloads/graph-benchmark-ldbc/expected-sf1.json: the 30 expected answers of neo4j/benchmark_query.py and which are
    order-sensitive.
  - src/schema.rs: the schema of neo4j/build_graph.py (labels, relationship types, the `ID` property, the CSV
    columns as properties); workloads/graph-benchmark-ldbc/indexes.cypher: the secondary indexes of ladybugdb/build_graph.py, plus
    two.

workloads/graph-benchmark-ldbc/expected-sf0.1.json is not from upstream (upstream publishes answers for SF1 only): it is the answers
a reference Neo4j run gave on the SF0.1 data set, recorded with the upstream
benchmark harness; its `_source` key holds the provenance.

Modification: at SF0.1 only, 14 of the queries run with literal values replaced (names, tags, places, IDs and one
threshold), as workloads/graph-benchmark-ldbc/literals-sf0.1.json lists with a reason for each (ADR-0247). The query files
themselves are upstream's text; SF1 runs them verbatim.

